import Lesson from "../../../../layouts/Lesson.astro";
const titlePt = "OAuth — o fluxo básico, visualmente";
const titleEn = "OAuth — the basic flow, visually";
const titleFallback = "OAuth flow";
const bodyClass = "lang-pt";
const assets = [
	"<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"../assets/style.css\" />",
	"<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"../assets/dark.css\" />",
	"<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"../assets/i18n.css\" />",
	"<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"../assets/concepts.css\" />",
	"<script src=\"../assets/i18n.js\" defer></script>",
	"<script src=\"../assets/nav.js\" defer></script>",
	"<script src=\"../assets/reading-ui.js\" defer></script>",
	"<script src=\"../assets/concepts.js\" defer></script>",
];

---
<Lesson
	titlePt={titlePt}
	titleEn={titleEn}
	titleFallback={titleFallback}
	bodyClass={bodyClass}
	assets={assets}
>
	<Fragment is:raw>
    <article class="lesson">
      <header class="hero">
        <span class="eyebrow">⬡ OAuth 2.0 · Authorization Code + PKCE</span>
        <h1>
          <span data-lang="pt">Dê acesso, não sua senha.</span
          ><span data-lang="en">Grant access, not your password.</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="lead">
          <span data-lang="pt"
            >Em 15 minutos: quem participa, como o código vira token e por que
            PKCE impede que um código roubado seja útil.</span
          ><span data-lang="en"
            >In 15 minutes: who participates, how a code becomes a token, and
            why PKCE makes a stolen code useless.</span
          >
        </p>
      </header>
      <nav class="concept-nav">
        <a href="0001-sql-foundations.html">← SQL</a
        ><a href="0002-oauth-flow.html">OAuth</a
        ><a href="0003-sql-sandbox.html">⌨ Sandbox</a
        ><a href="../reference/software-concepts-cheatsheet.html"
          ><span data-lang="pt">Folha rápida</span
          ><span data-lang="en">Cheat sheet</span></a
        ><a href="../../../index.html">Hub</a>
      </nav>

      <h2 class="section">
        <span class="num">1</span
        ><span data-lang="pt">Primeiro: OAuth não é login</span
        ><span data-lang="en">First: OAuth is not login</span>
      </h2>
      <p>
        <span data-lang="pt"
          >OAuth é um framework de <strong>autorização delegada</strong>: um
          aplicativo recebe permissão limitada para agir sobre recursos do
          usuário sem receber sua senha. “Login com…” normalmente adiciona
          OpenID Connect para autenticação.</span
        ><span data-lang="en"
          >OAuth is a framework for <strong>delegated authorization</strong>: an
          app gets limited permission to act on a user's resources without
          receiving the password. “Sign in with…” normally adds OpenID Connect
          for authentication.</span
        >
      </p>
      <div class="callout warn">
        <p>
          <span data-lang="pt"
            ><strong>Pergunta diferente:</strong> autenticação = “quem é você?”;
            autorização = “o que este app pode fazer?”</span
          ><span data-lang="en"
            ><strong>Different question:</strong> authentication = “who are
            you?”; authorization = “what may this app do?”</span
          >
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2 class="section">
        <span class="num">2</span
        ><span data-lang="pt">Os quatro participantes</span
        ><span data-lang="en">The four participants</span>
      </h2>
      <div class="actors">
        <div class="actor">
          <span class="icon">🧑</span
          ><strong
            ><span data-lang="pt">Dono do recurso</span
            ><span data-lang="en">Resource owner</span></strong
          ><br /><small
            ><span data-lang="pt">você</span
            ><span data-lang="en">you</span></small
          >
        </div>
        <div class="actor">
          <span class="icon">📱</span><strong>Client</strong><br /><small
            ><span data-lang="pt">app pedindo acesso</span
            ><span data-lang="en">app requesting access</span></small
          >
        </div>
        <div class="actor">
          <span class="icon">🪪</span><strong>Authorization server</strong
          ><br /><small
            ><span data-lang="pt">login, consentimento, tokens</span
            ><span data-lang="en">login, consent, tokens</span></small
          >
        </div>
        <div class="actor">
          <span class="icon">🗄️</span><strong>Resource server</strong
          ><br /><small
            ><span data-lang="pt">API protegida</span
            ><span data-lang="en">protected API</span></small
          >
        </div>
      </div>
      <p>
        <span data-lang="pt"
          >O cliente nunca precisa ver a senha:
          <strong
            >o usuário autentica diretamente no servidor de autorização</strong
          >.</span
        ><span data-lang="en"
          >The client never needs the password:
          <strong
            >the user authenticates directly with the authorization
            server</strong
          >.</span
        >
      </p>
      <p class="cite-line">
        <span data-lang="pt">Definições oficiais:</span
        ><span data-lang="en">Official definitions:</span>
        <a href="https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc6749#section-1.1"
          >RFC 6749 §1.1</a
        >.
      </p>

      <h2 class="section">
        <span class="num">3</span><span data-lang="pt">Percorra o fluxo</span
        ><span data-lang="en">Walk through the flow</span>
      </h2>
      <p>
        <span data-lang="pt"
          >Clique em “próximo”. Observe que o navegador transporta um
          <em>código curto e descartável</em>; o access token chega no token
          endpoint, não na URL de autorização.</span
        ><span data-lang="en"
          >Click “next”. Notice that the browser carries a
          <em>short-lived, disposable code</em>; the access token arrives from
          the token endpoint, not in the authorization URL.</span
        >
      </p>
      <div class="flow-board" data-flow>
        <div class="flow-row">
          <span class="step">1</span>
          <div>
            <strong>Client → Authorization server</strong><br /><span
              data-lang="pt"
              >Redireciona com <code>client_id</code>,
              <code>redirect_uri</code>, <code>scope</code>,
              <code>state</code> e desafio PKCE.</span
            ><span data-lang="en"
              >Redirects with <code>client_id</code>, <code>redirect_uri</code>,
              <code>scope</code>, <code>state</code>, and a PKCE
              challenge.</span
            >
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="flow-row">
          <span class="step">2</span>
          <div>
            <strong>User ↔ Authorization server</strong><br /><span
              data-lang="pt"
              >O usuário faz login e aprova o escopo pedido.</span
            ><span data-lang="en"
              >The user signs in and approves the requested scope.</span
            >
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="flow-row">
          <span class="step">3</span>
          <div>
            <strong>Authorization server → Client callback</strong><br /><span
              data-lang="pt"
              >Redireciona para a URI registrada com
              <span class="token">code</span> + <code>state</code>.</span
            ><span data-lang="en"
              >Redirects to the registered URI with a
              <span class="token">code</span> + <code>state</code>.</span
            >
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="flow-row">
          <span class="step">4</span>
          <div>
            <strong>Client → Token endpoint</strong><br /><span data-lang="pt"
              >Troca <code>code</code> + <code>code_verifier</code> por
              tokens.</span
            ><span data-lang="en"
              >Exchanges <code>code</code> + <code>code_verifier</code> for
              tokens.</span
            >
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="flow-row">
          <span class="step">5</span>
          <div>
            <strong>Client → Resource server</strong><br /><span data-lang="pt"
              >Chama a API com
              <code>Authorization: Bearer &lt;access_token&gt;</code>.</span
            ><span data-lang="en"
              >Calls the API with
              <code>Authorization: Bearer &lt;access_token&gt;</code>.</span
            >
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="flow-row">
          <span class="step">6</span>
          <div>
            <strong>Resource server → Client</strong><br /><span data-lang="pt"
              >Valida token e escopo; devolve o recurso permitido.</span
            ><span data-lang="en"
              >Validates token and scope; returns the permitted resource.</span
            >
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="flow-controls">
          <button type="button" data-next>
            <span data-lang="pt">Próximo →</span
            ><span data-lang="en">Next →</span></button
          ><button type="button" data-reset>
            <span data-lang="pt">Reiniciar</span
            ><span data-lang="en">Reset</span></button
          ><span data-flow-status aria-live="polite"></span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="cite-line">
        <span data-lang="pt">Fluxo-base:</span
        ><span data-lang="en">Base flow:</span>
        <a href="https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc6749#section-4.1"
          >RFC 6749 §4.1</a
        >.
      </p>

      <h2 class="section">
        <span class="num">4</span><span data-lang="pt">Código não é token</span
        ><span data-lang="en">A code is not a token</span>
      </h2>
      <div class="mental-model">
        <div class="concept-card">
          <h3>Authorization code</h3>
          <p>
            <span data-lang="pt"
              >Uso único, vida curta, só serve para a troca.</span
            ><span data-lang="en"
              >One-time, short-lived, useful only for exchange.</span
            >
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="concept-card">
          <h3>Access token</h3>
          <p>
            <span data-lang="pt"
              >Credencial apresentada à API; limitado por escopo e tempo.</span
            ><span data-lang="en"
              >Credential presented to the API; limited by scope and
              lifetime.</span
            >
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="concept-card">
          <h3>Refresh token</h3>
          <p>
            <span data-lang="pt"
              >Opcional; obtém novo access token sem novo consentimento.</span
            ><span data-lang="en"
              >Optional; gets a new access token without new consent.</span
            >
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p>
        <span data-lang="pt"
          ><strong>Trate tokens como credenciais</strong>: não coloque access
          tokens em URLs, logs ou armazenamento inseguro.</span
        ><span data-lang="en"
          ><strong>Treat tokens as credentials</strong>: do not put access
          tokens in URLs, logs, or insecure storage.</span
        >
      </p>

      <h2 class="section">
        <span class="num">5</span>PKCE:
        <span data-lang="pt">a prova de posse</span
        ><span data-lang="en">proof of possession</span>
      </h2>
      <p>
        <span data-lang="pt"
          >Antes do redirect, o cliente cria um segredo aleatório
          <code>verifier</code> e envia apenas seu hash <code>challenge</code>.
          Na troca, revela o verifier. O servidor recalcula o hash.
          <strong>Um código interceptado não basta sem o verifier</strong
          >.</span
        ><span data-lang="en"
          >Before redirecting, the client creates a random
          <code>verifier</code> and sends only its hashed
          <code>challenge</code>. During exchange it reveals the verifier. The
          server hashes it again.
          <strong>An intercepted code is useless without the verifier</strong
          >.</span
        >
      </p>
      <div class="schema">
        <div class="db-table">
          <b>Client keeps</b>
          <div class="db-row match">
            <span>verifier</span><span>🎲 secret</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="join-link">SHA-256 →</div>
        <div class="db-table">
          <b>Server receives first</b>
          <div class="db-row match">
            <span>challenge</span><span># hash</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="security-pair">
        <div class="concept-card danger">
          <h3>
            😈 <span data-lang="pt">Atacante</span
            ><span data-lang="en">Attacker</span>
          </h3>
          <p>
            <span data-lang="pt"
              >Rouba o <code>code</code>, mas não conhece o verifier: troca
              recusada.</span
            ><span data-lang="en"
              >Steals the <code>code</code>, but lacks the verifier: exchange
              rejected.</span
            >
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="concept-card safe">
          <h3>✅ Client</h3>
          <p>
            <span data-lang="pt"
              >Apresenta code + verifier correto: recebe o token.</span
            ><span data-lang="en"
              >Presents code + correct verifier: receives the token.</span
            >
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="cite-line">
        <a href="https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc7636#section-4"
          >RFC 7636 §4</a
        >
        ·
        <a href="https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc9700#section-2.1.1"
          >RFC 9700 §2.1.1</a
        >
        <span data-lang="pt"
          >requer PKCE para clientes públicos e recomenda para clientes
          confidenciais.</span
        ><span data-lang="en"
          >requires PKCE for public clients and recommends it for confidential
          clients.</span
        >
      </p>

      <h2 class="section">
        <span class="num">6</span
        ><span data-lang="pt">Cheque sua explicação</span
        ><span data-lang="en">Check your explanation</span>
      </h2>
      <details>
        <summary>
          <span data-lang="pt"
            >Por que redirecionar para o authorization server?</span
          ><span data-lang="en">Why redirect to the authorization server?</span>
        </summary>
        <p>
          <span data-lang="pt"
            >Para que credenciais e consentimento fiquem com a autoridade
            confiável; o client recebe delegação, não a senha.</span
          ><span data-lang="en"
            >So credentials and consent stay with the trusted authority; the
            client receives delegation, not the password.</span
          >
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>
          <span data-lang="pt">O que scope controla?</span
          ><span data-lang="en">What does scope control?</span>
        </summary>
        <p>
          <span data-lang="pt"
            >A extensão do acesso delegado, por exemplo
            <code>photos:read</code> sem <code>photos:delete</code>.</span
          ><span data-lang="en"
            >The extent of delegated access, for example
            <code>photos:read</code> without <code>photos:delete</code>.</span
          >
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>
          <span data-lang="pt">OAuth faz autenticação?</span
          ><span data-lang="en">Does OAuth authenticate?</span>
        </summary>
        <p>
          <span data-lang="pt"
            >Não sozinho. OAuth autoriza acesso. OpenID Connect adiciona
            identidade/autenticação sobre OAuth.</span
          ><span data-lang="en"
            >Not by itself. OAuth authorizes access. OpenID Connect adds
            identity/authentication on top of OAuth.</span
          >
        </p>
      </details>
      <div class="callout key">
        <p>
          <strong
            ><span data-lang="pt">Resposta de entrevista em 20 segundos:</span
            ><span data-lang="en">20-second interview answer:</span></strong
          >
          <span data-lang="pt"
            >“O client redireciona o usuário ao authorization server para login
            e consentimento. Recebe um código curto no callback, valida state e
            troca código + PKCE verifier por um access token. Usa esse token,
            limitado por scope, para chamar a API. Assim o app nunca recebe a
            senha do usuário.”</span
          ><span data-lang="en"
            >“The client redirects the user to the authorization server for
            sign-in and consent. It receives a short-lived code at its callback,
            validates state, and exchanges the code plus PKCE verifier for an
            access token. It uses that scoped token to call the API, so the app
            never receives the user's password.”</span
          >
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="callout info">
        <p>
          <span data-lang="pt"
            >Quer mapear isso para Next.js, Node ou uma SPA?
            <strong
              >Pergunte ao agente; a localização segura dos tokens depende da
              arquitetura.</strong
            ></span
          ><span data-lang="en"
            >Want to map this to Next.js, Node, or an SPA?
            <strong
              >Ask the agent; safe token placement depends on the
              architecture.</strong
            ></span
          >
        </p>
      </div>
      <p class="cite-line">
        <span data-lang="pt">Leitura principal:</span
        ><span data-lang="en">Primary reading:</span>
        <a href="https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc9700#section-2.1"
          >OAuth 2.0 Security Best Current Practice §2.1</a
        >.
        <a href="../reference/software-concepts-cheatsheet.html"
          ><span data-lang="pt">Revisar folha rápida →</span
          ><span data-lang="en">Review cheat sheet →</span></a
        >
      </p>
    </article>
  </Fragment>
</Lesson>
